# WashGo monetization + promotion backend

This repo now includes:
- a monetization panel in `index.html`
- a promote button on each wash card
- a small Stripe Checkout backend example in `server.js`

## Quick start

1. Install dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

2. Set your Stripe secret key and public URL:

```bash
export STRIPE_SECRET_KEY="sk_live_..."
export PUBLIC_URL="https://your-frontend-domain.com"
```

3. Start the backend:

```bash
npm start
```

4. In the frontend, point the app to your backend by setting this in the browser before the page loads:

```html
<script>
  window.WASHGO_PROMOTION_API_BASE = 'https://your-backend-domain.com';
</script>
```

If you host the frontend and backend on the same domain, you can leave the default `fetch('/create-promotion')` behavior as-is.

## Files added

- `server.js` — Express + Stripe backend example
- `index.html` — monetization UI and promote flow
- `package.json` — starter scripts and dependencies

## Payment flow

- visitor clicks `Promote`
- app posts to `/create-promotion`
- backend creates a Stripe Checkout Session
- user is redirected to Stripe
- on success, your app can read the `session_id` and mark the listing as promoted

## Recommended production follow-up

- add a database to persist promoted listings and expiry dates
- add a Stripe webhook to confirm successful payments and activate promotions
- add an admin dashboard to review and manage promotion status
- swap placeholder donation links and ad slot with real links / AdSense publisher info

## Deployment options

- Render: deploy the Node app as a web service
- Railway: deploy directly from GitHub
- Heroku: deploy the app with `npm start`
- VPS / Docker: run `node server.js`

## Notes

- Stripe charges in cents, so example pricing is set as `R50 = 5000`, `R90 = 9000`, `R150 = 15000` in ZAR.
- Replace `YOUR_USERNAME` and `YOUR_PAYPAL` in `index.html` with your real profiles before going live.
